# Tauri
src-tauri/target/
# gen/ is regenerated scratch EXCEPT four hand-customized files: three on
# Android (CAMERA permission + soft-keyboard fix + dual-keystore signing block)
# and the iOS Info.plist. Git can't re-include a file whose parent dir is
# excluded, hence the level-by-level carve-out below. Keystore properties,
# build output, the rest of gen/apple and wry's generated/ stay ignored.
#
# The iOS plist is here for CFBundleLocalizations. WKWebView reports the app's
# EFFECTIVE locale to `navigator.language`, which iOS computes by intersecting
# the phone's preferred languages with the languages the bundle declares - so
# an undeclared language makes a German phone report `en`, and the app seeds
# English starter notes and English UI for a user who asked for neither.
# Nothing fails when that array is lost: the app builds, runs, and is quietly
# wrong for every non-English user. Android has no such gate, which is why only
# iOS needs this. `scripts/sync-version.mjs` writes the array from
# SUPPORTED_LOCALES in `packages/web/src/i18n.ts` before every build (`zh-TW`
# is declared as `zh-Hant` there, the tag iOS knows).
#
# Extended 2026-08-28: the private repo is now the full dev-environment backup,
# so the hand-editable platform config joins the carve-out. The test is whether
# a fresh clone can rebuild the file. Tauri regenerates tauri.properties,
# tauri.build.gradle.kts, proguard-tauri.pro and tauri.settings.gradle from
# tracked config on every build, so those stay out and cause no churn. The
# signing keystores and their property files stay out for good.
src-tauri/gen/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/
src-tauri/gen/android/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/build.gradle.kts
!src-tauri/gen/android/gradle.properties
!src-tauri/gen/android/settings.gradle
!src-tauri/gen/android/gradlew
!src-tauri/gen/android/gradlew.bat
!src-tauri/gen/android/gradle/
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/build.gradle.kts
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/proguard-rules.pro
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/app/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/app/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/app/privacynotes/
src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/app/privacynotes/*
!src-tauri/gen/android/app/src/main/java/app/privacynotes/MainActivity.kt
!src-tauri/gen/apple/
src-tauri/gen/apple/*
!src-tauri/gen/apple/ExportOptions.plist
!src-tauri/gen/apple/project.yml
!src-tauri/gen/apple/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy
!src-tauri/gen/apple/LaunchScreen.storyboard
!src-tauri/gen/apple/Podfile
!src-tauri/gen/apple/Assets.xcassets/
!src-tauri/gen/apple/privacynotes_iOS/
src-tauri/gen/apple/privacynotes_iOS/*
!src-tauri/gen/apple/privacynotes_iOS/Info.plist
!src-tauri/gen/apple/privacynotes_iOS/privacynotes_iOS.entitlements
# Cargo.lock IS committed (this is an app, not a library) for reproducible release builds - do not re-ignore it
